     1	//! `ql-udf` — out-of-process Python UDF worker transport + codec.
     2	//!
     3	//! **Phase 6.4-3 (the wedge).** Design: `docs/phase6/6-4-3-design.md`. This crate
     4	//! owns the *mechanics* of talking to a managed Python worker process: the wire
     5	//! protocol (length-prefixed frames), the Arrow ↔ engine-`Value` codec, and the
     6	//! [`UdfWorker`] abstraction. It is a **leaf** (dependency-inversion, mirroring
     7	//! `ql-io-csv` / `ql-io-xlsx`): it depends only on `ql-types`, `arrow`, and
     8	//! `thiserror`, and is consumed by `ql-exec` at the dispatch site (6.4-3c), which
     9	//! adapts `FunctionArg`/`FunctionReturn` ↔ [`ql_types::ArrayValue`] and injects a
    10	//! worker into the eval context.
    11	//!
    12	//! **6.4-3a scope (this cycle — Rust-only, no Python, no subprocess):**
    13	//! - [`codec`] — `ArrayValue` ⇄ Arrow IPC stream bytes (the "fiddly part", with
    14	//!   round-trip property tests over every `Value` variant).
    15	//! - [`frame`] — the `[u32 LE len][u8 type][payload]` envelope + [`frame::FrameType`].
    16	//! - [`worker`] — the [`worker::UdfWorker`] trait + an in-process
    17	//!   [`worker::MockWorker`] (proves call / raise / timeout mapping without a
    18	//!   subprocess) + the [`worker::UdfError`] taxonomy.
    19	//!
    20	//! **Deliberately deferred** (later 6.4-3 cycles): real subprocess spawn /
    21	//! handshake / kill (6.4-3b); the eval-site `RegisteredFn::Udf` dispatch arm
    22	//! (6.4-3c); debugpy + trusted-workspace gating (6.4-3d). The control-frame
    23	//! payload internals (Hello/Raise/Log field encodings) are intentionally opaque
    24	//! `Vec<u8>` at this layer until 6.4-3b pins the worker handshake.
    25	//!
    26	//! The on-wire batch format is Arrow IPC (chosen so the Python side uses
    27	//! `pyarrow` natively); the [`codec`] boundary keeps it swappable.
    28	
    29	pub mod codec;
    30	pub mod frame;
    31	pub mod worker;
    32	
    33	pub use frame::{Frame, FrameType};
    34	pub use worker::{MockWorker, UdfError, UdfWorker};

